 # Engel E2 — blackboard parity invariant
 
+## source statement (R6 fix, 2026-09-08)
+
+> Suppose the positive integer n is odd. First Al writes the numbers 1, 2, ..., 2n on the
+> blackboard. Then he picks any two numbers a, b, erases them, and writes |a - b|. Prove
+> that an odd number will remain at the end.
+
+Authoritative text: `training_records/engel_e2_blackboard_parity.yaml` — the statement the
+machine sees. Quoted here verbatim per the R6 ruling: the loadable record's YAML text is
+authoritative; cards quote it, never paraphrase it. The card's previous opening was a
+paraphrase and is demoted to prose:
+
 Numbers `1, 2, ..., 2n` stand on a board. A move erases two of them, `a` and `b`, and writes
 `|a - b|`. When `n` is odd, the last remaining number is odd.
 
